<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<%- include('../partials/head') %>
<title>Recovery — HeartCode Admin</title>
</head>
<body data-page="recovery">
<div class="admin-shell">
  <%- include('../partials/nav', { activePage: 'recovery' }) %>
  <main class="admin-main">
    <h1 class="mb-1 font-display text-2xl uppercase tracking-wide text-hc-ink">Pending Deployment Recovery</h1>
    <p class="mb-4 text-sm text-slate-500">
      A checkout row is kept for 7 days after it expires before it's automatically cleaned up — long enough to recover
      a payment that succeeded but whose webhook never fired and whose client never landed back on the confirmation page.
      "Check &amp; Deploy" is safe to click on any row: it re-verifies with Paystack first and does nothing unless that
      verification actually succeeds.
    </p>
    <div class="admin-card mb-4 max-w-md">
      <label class="admin-label" for="recoverySearch">Search</label>
      <input class="admin-input" type="text" id="recoverySearch" placeholder="Email or reference">
    </div>
    <div class="admin-table-wrap">
      <table class="admin-table is-responsive-stack">
        <thead><tr><th>Reference</th><th>Client</th><th>Type</th><th>Amount</th><th>Created</th><th>Status</th><th></th></tr></thead>
        <tbody id="recoveryTableBody"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-2 flex items-center justify-between">
      <p id="recoveryPageInfo" class="text-xs text-slate-400"></p>
      <div class="flex gap-2">
        <button type="button" id="recoveryPrev" class="admin-btn-outline admin-btn-sm">← Prev</button>
        <button type="button" id="recoveryNext" class="admin-btn-outline admin-btn-sm">Next →</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</div>
</body>
</html>
